        author = "This catalogue, as a proposal (not an established model)",
        year = 2026,
        summary = "A publicly funded place for every child before compulsory school, with fees capped by household income and free for the lowest incomes. Public, non-profit and licensed providers meet national standards, and the state funds the full cost of the cap.",
        details = "Keeps: income-linked fees from Nordic social democracy (Sweden's fee cap on preschool and after-school care (maxtaxa), enacted amounts unconfirmed), and free places with meals and jobs for unemployed adults from Keynesian welfare capitalism (Nursery schools of the New Deal (FERA and WPA), secondary-source figures to be checked). Blocks: fee rises where state funding falls short, blocked by a fully funded cap; lower language scores and costs above returns, blocked by early-learning standards and a cost review (that evidence comes from working papers, and the 2013 study is non-experimental); exclusion of poor families, blocked by a fee-free place for the lowest incomes. Test: places for children aged two to five, fees relative to income, and language at school entry against a comparison group, over the years after each change. Source: Riksdag written question on evaluating the maxtaxa (2004); CIRPEE working paper 08-23 (2008); CIRPEE working paper 13-34 (2013); Living New Deal, The Crisis of Childcare and the profile of Grace Langdon (secondary web sources); Smith, The Wealth of Nations (1776).",
    ),
)
